1
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:29,154
FROM ME TO YOU: KIMI NI TODOKE
3RD SEASON

2
00:01:22,415 --> 00:01:24,959
The class trip
was a whole lot of fun.

3
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:28,963
And the biggest event of our second year
of high school... is over.

4
00:01:29,047 --> 00:01:31,382
Man, those pineapples
were so good!

5
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:34,803
So the second day,
we went to the aquarium, had pineapples,

6
00:01:34,886 --> 00:01:36,304
went to Cape Manzamo...

7
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:37,639
And was that it?

8
00:01:37,722 --> 00:01:40,975
Oh, and then we had
a little bit of free time that night.

9
00:01:41,059 --> 00:01:42,936
I remember, 'cause you and Mogi-cchi...

10
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:46,439
What's wrong?

11
00:01:46,523 --> 00:01:48,358
It's, uh... how do I say it?

12
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:50,193
That sure was fast, eh?

13
00:01:50,276 --> 00:01:53,988
It's fine.
There's nothing I coulda done.

14
00:01:54,072 --> 00:01:56,908
And it'd be a pain
to have you both tiptoe around me.

15
00:01:56,991 --> 00:02:01,121
Besides, looking back on it now,
he wasn't my type at all. The end.

16
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:03,540
P-- pretty sure
you're actually pissed.

17
00:02:04,165 --> 00:02:05,041
- Uh...
- Hmm?

18
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:07,335
...was this Ryukyu Village?

19
00:02:07,418 --> 00:02:08,795
Let me see.

20
00:02:08,878 --> 00:02:11,131
Oh wow! Look at that face!

21
00:02:12,215 --> 00:02:15,426
This was right after she got confronted
by that girl from Class--

22
00:02:19,013 --> 00:02:20,390
Argh!

23
00:02:20,473 --> 00:02:22,225
You didn't have to rip it up like that!

24
00:02:22,308 --> 00:02:24,811
C'mon! The look on your face
was pure gold!

25
00:02:24,894 --> 00:02:26,938
I did. I don't need the reminder.

26
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:30,775
Okay, but you weren't
the only one in the picture, you know!

27
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:35,113
Yeah, you're right.

28
00:02:35,196 --> 00:02:37,657
Sawako was in that one too. Sorry.

29
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:40,910
- Oh...
- Wha--

30
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:42,787
Oh, look, I ripped through Ryu.

31
00:02:43,371 --> 00:02:45,748
Speaking of, how have things been
between you two?

32
00:02:46,332 --> 00:02:48,001
Uh. Normal.

33
00:02:48,084 --> 00:02:50,086
We talk and hang at his place...

34
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:52,046
So pretty much the same as before.

35
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:53,590
Oh, that's right.

36
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:55,925
His birthday's coming up next month.

37
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:56,843
Gift, huh?

38
00:02:56,926 --> 00:02:59,804
If you ask me, you might as well
just start dating already.

39
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:00,722
What?!

40
00:03:00,805 --> 00:03:04,100
I mean, it really makes no difference
whether you two are going out or not.

41
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:05,476
It's still you and Ryu.

42
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,937
Huh?! You could not be more off base!

43
00:03:08,021 --> 00:03:09,856
You don't get it, do you, Yano-chin?

44
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:11,691
I mean, if we started dating,
that would mean

45
00:03:12,525 --> 00:03:14,569
k-- kissing and stuff like that!

46
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:19,782
Hmm?

47
00:03:21,159 --> 00:03:25,496
- Did you...?
- No. We definitely haven't. Seriously!

48
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:28,541
So, I don't get it,
what's wrong with you and Ryu kissing?

49
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:30,460
- Everything!
- Huh? You totally could.

50
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:31,878
Not in a million years!

51
00:03:33,588 --> 00:03:37,842
It's just that...
I've never seen him that way. Ever.

52
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:40,261
What if we dated and broke up?

53
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:43,181
- I don't wanna think about it.
- 'Kay, then don't break up.

54
00:03:43,264 --> 00:03:45,558
Who's the one
who broke up with Mogi right away?

55
00:03:47,185 --> 00:03:49,187
It's never even crossed my mind.

56
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:52,398
And I just don't want to change
what we have going for us now.

57
00:03:52,982 --> 00:03:54,067
Anyway.

58
00:03:54,776 --> 00:03:56,736
I was in love with Toru, remember?

59
00:03:58,071 --> 00:04:00,073
After our big class trip ended,

60
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:04,577
a lot of things were
a little different than they were before.

61
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:10,124
First, Ayane decided
not to go out with Mogi anymore.

62
00:04:12,168 --> 00:04:14,254
- Hey, Chizuru?
- Hmm?

63
00:04:15,129 --> 00:04:19,550
Here. Pin says you need to bring this
back to him after school. Redone.

64
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:24,180
Then Chizu decided she wasn't
going to go out with Sanada after all.

65
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:25,223
What is it?

66
00:04:25,306 --> 00:04:27,058
It's my career questionnaire.

67
00:04:28,768 --> 00:04:30,186
Wow! What a moron!

68
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:32,021
It's just that I haven't decided!

69
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:34,023
As for me...

70
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:36,776
- Uh, hey, Kazehaya.
- Hmm?

71
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:38,236
I've got a present for you.

72
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:40,613
Uh? A picture? For me?

73
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,156
Thanks!

74
00:04:42,824 --> 00:04:45,702
It's of Sawako in her undies.

75
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:49,372
Oh, please.
I'm obviously kidding, you dork!

76
00:04:49,455 --> 00:04:51,916
- Sorry to rain on your parade.
- Wha--

77
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,752
- You can have it though.
- I don't want it!

78
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:57,171
Oh, it's me.

79
00:04:57,255 --> 00:05:00,425
It's not like
I don't want any photos of you, Kuronuma.

80
00:05:00,508 --> 00:05:02,760
Man, your boyfriend sure is awful, huh?

81
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:05,763
This has nothing
to do with you! I'll take it!

82
00:05:05,847 --> 00:05:06,681
I'll take it.

83
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:09,350
Thanks for this.

84
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:13,771
Sawako and Kazehaya
are the same as ever, huh?

85
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:14,731
Uh-huh.

86
00:05:15,398 --> 00:05:16,607
Uh--

87
00:05:31,622 --> 00:05:36,169
On my end, Kazehaya and I
aren't chatting quite as much.

88
00:05:37,337 --> 00:05:39,964
And I could just be imagining things,

89
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:44,385
but he also... doesn't seem to look my way
all that often.

90
00:05:47,388 --> 00:05:50,391
Needless to say, he doesn't hold my hand.

91
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:59,233
It feels like there's
a little more distance between us now.

92
00:05:59,317 --> 00:06:01,069
Sawa... ko.

93
00:06:01,652 --> 00:06:03,279
Sh-- Shota.

94
00:06:04,822 --> 00:06:07,950
Hey. Close your eyes.

95
00:06:10,119 --> 00:06:11,496
The days...

96
00:06:11,579 --> 00:06:12,997
...are getting shorter, huh?

97
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,543
Uh... mmm.

98
00:06:21,047 --> 00:06:24,217
Wait, am I expecting more than I should?!

99
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:27,470
Like holding hands,

100
00:06:28,012 --> 00:06:29,806
using our first names,

101
00:06:29,889 --> 00:06:32,809
closing some of the distance between us?

102
00:06:32,892 --> 00:06:37,688
Were those things,
like the summer and Okinawa... fleeting?

103
00:06:37,772 --> 00:06:41,067
Like a mirage that we saw
because of the season's heat,

104
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:43,152
too exhilarating to last?

105
00:06:48,699 --> 00:06:52,161
Summer is over, and fall will pass soon.

106
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:57,625
Then the second winter since I met
everyone will be right around the corner.

107
00:06:57,708 --> 00:07:02,630
EPISODE 3
GIRLFRIEND AND BOYFRIEND

108
00:07:05,716 --> 00:07:10,012
- Oh, you're Ayane, right?
- Uh, who are...

109
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:12,473
Oh! Kento Girls, right?

110
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:16,227
- She called us Kento Girls!
- What does she mean by that?

111
00:07:16,894 --> 00:07:21,274
Hey, in Okinawa, you were hanging out
and chatting with Kento for a bit, right?

112
00:07:22,233 --> 00:07:25,319
- You mean on the free day, or...
- Yeah, exactly.

113
00:07:25,403 --> 00:07:29,282
I remember it was when we were
all chilling with Kento and Tsuru, right?

114
00:07:29,365 --> 00:07:30,575
What is this?

115
00:07:30,658 --> 00:07:32,118
The thing they did to Chizu?

116
00:07:32,201 --> 00:07:33,661
Are they feeling me out?

117
00:07:33,744 --> 00:07:36,581
So, Ayane.
Can we ask if you like Kento?

118
00:07:36,664 --> 00:07:38,291
Yep, here it comes.

119
00:07:38,374 --> 00:07:40,626
No, but I don't dislike him either.

120
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:41,919
Oh, really?!

121
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:43,546
Huh?

122
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:46,591
You see, we heard
you went through a breakup.

123
00:07:46,674 --> 00:07:48,342
- Mm-hmm.
- That must've been rough.

124
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:51,429
Actually, I recently broke up
with my boyfriend too.

125
00:07:51,512 --> 00:07:54,474
What?!
Who told you about that? Kento?

126
00:07:54,557 --> 00:07:56,058
No. Just rumors.

127
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:58,227
Kento never gossips
about that stuff.

128
00:07:58,311 --> 00:08:00,897
Right? He's an ally to all girls.

129
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:04,817
Uh, so, is it that
all of you like Kento, then?

130
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:06,861
And then you're also all friends?

131
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:09,155
I don't understand how that can work.

132
00:08:09,238 --> 00:08:10,323
What?!

133
00:08:10,406 --> 00:08:13,951
I mean, we all just adore Kento
because he's so genuinely kind.

134
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:16,245
Like, back when I got dumped
by my boyfriend,

135
00:08:16,329 --> 00:08:19,540
Kento went through it with me
and let me vent as much as I needed to.

136
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:22,710
For me, it was when
I wasn't getting along with mine.

137
00:08:22,793 --> 00:08:25,004
My boyfriend actually goes
to another school,

138
00:08:25,087 --> 00:08:27,089
but Kento gives me all kinds of advice.

139
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:29,717
It's really nice to have
a boy around like that.

140
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,385
I love having girlfriends too,

141
00:08:31,469 --> 00:08:34,138
but boys just fill a different
kind of space, ya know?

142
00:08:34,222 --> 00:08:37,934
Since we always hang out
as a group, it's not cheating. It's fun.

143
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:39,769
It makes us feel so much better.

144
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:40,853
So...

145
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:41,979
...if you're up for it,

146
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:45,983
you should join us sometime,
so we can have a good time together.

147
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:48,236
It'll be fun! It'll be fun!

148
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:50,571
- It'll be... fun?
-   It'll be fun!

149
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:55,284
Close call! If I'm not careful,
I'll end up becoming a Kento Girl!

150
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:58,246
Oh no, I think I'll be fine
on my own for now, but thanks!

151
00:08:58,329 --> 00:09:00,122
Ahh!

152
00:09:01,165 --> 00:09:02,792
- But, hey...
- Hmm?

153
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:07,255
Don't any of you
ever get any romantic feelings for Kento?

154
00:09:07,338 --> 00:09:10,174
You must have at least thought about
going out with him or something.

155
00:09:10,258 --> 00:09:12,343
Hmm. Well, let me think about it.

156
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:15,805
- I wouldn't mind that, but...
- It's true that we all love him a lot,

157
00:09:15,888 --> 00:09:19,183
and flipping the switch from platonic
to not wouldn't be very hard, but...

158
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:22,270
there's not another person
that could fill that role, so...

159
00:09:22,353 --> 00:09:25,147
Then, what if Kento found someone?

160
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,899
Like a girlfriend?!

161
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:29,735
Yeah, that's true.
'Cause he's single now, isn't he?

162
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:32,363
There was a time
when he was dating someone, right?

163
00:09:32,446 --> 00:09:34,532
Yeah, and it was more than just once too.

164
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:36,659
Oh, so in other words...

165
00:09:36,742 --> 00:09:39,829
That wouldn't really
change anything for us, probably.

166
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:41,914
Hmm.

167
00:09:45,209 --> 00:09:47,753
There's no replacing Kento, huh?

168
00:09:48,462 --> 00:09:52,466
I had no idea, but I guess
Kento's actually pretty widely loved.

169
00:09:56,929 --> 00:09:59,181
Please.

170
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:01,517
Hm.

171
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:28,294
Oh.

172
00:10:31,547 --> 00:10:33,674
Oh, I guess that's his train.

173
00:11:02,995 --> 00:11:04,205
Ayane.

174
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:08,709
The hell?!

175
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:11,504
I thought you were long gone by now!
Stay away from me!

176
00:11:11,587 --> 00:11:15,091
Ouch! That stings. But at least
I know you're the same old Ayane.

177
00:11:15,174 --> 00:11:17,385
I'm glad I stayed here.

178
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:22,098
So, you've been avoiding me, haven't you?

179
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:25,476
Hm.

180
00:11:29,605 --> 00:11:31,524
I was embarrassed, so yeah.

181
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:35,653
Don't act surprised!

182
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:38,489
You've been totally watching me
since all that happened.

183
00:11:39,156 --> 00:11:42,660
Anyway, it's not like
I normally cry that much or anything.

184
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:44,120
It's just...

185
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:46,831
Uh, but don't get me wrong,

186
00:11:46,914 --> 00:11:50,084
that doesn't mean I was taking it
particularly hard either, so...

187
00:12:05,683 --> 00:12:07,268
Here. It's a warm one.

188
00:12:08,394 --> 00:12:09,353
Thank you.

189
00:12:10,229 --> 00:12:11,272
No prob.

190
00:12:12,481 --> 00:12:13,733
I see.

191
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:18,028
So this is how someone
gets turned into a Kento Girl.

192
00:12:19,405 --> 00:12:21,824
Right now, I think I get how they feel.

193
00:12:21,907 --> 00:12:23,659
I mean, he's not a bad guy.

194
00:12:24,410 --> 00:12:26,746
He's actually gentle and kind.

195
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:30,124
Do you know why
I'm always watching you, Ayane?

196
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:48,350
The train on Platform 2
will be departing soon.

197
00:12:48,434 --> 00:12:49,643
Please watch your step.

198
00:13:10,998 --> 00:13:12,416
Chizu!

199
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:15,586
Here are those sushi rolls!
Take them over to Ryu's, will ya?

200
00:13:15,669 --> 00:13:17,755
Oh. Mm-hmm.

201
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:23,761
Huh?

202
00:13:23,844 --> 00:13:26,263
Hold on a second, Yoshida rejected you?

203
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:28,724
Uh-huh. Didn't I tell you?

204
00:13:28,808 --> 00:13:33,145
No. I-- it's fine, but...
are you two okay after that?

205
00:13:33,854 --> 00:13:38,234
Yeah, I mean, I knew that Chizuru
would react that way right off the bat.

206
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:41,737
So, in a way, I feel relieved.

207
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:45,449
Since that person

208
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:48,118
was always you.

209
00:13:49,078 --> 00:13:50,079
Always?

210
00:13:50,913 --> 00:13:52,206
Always, since when?

211
00:13:54,166 --> 00:13:55,167
Always...

212
00:13:55,709 --> 00:13:58,921
Honestly, I'm glad that
it came down to this.

213
00:13:59,672 --> 00:14:02,883
'Cause now you can move on
and have your own life.

214
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:04,969
That time too?

215
00:14:05,469 --> 00:14:08,097
You really did love him.
I know you did.

216
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:09,932
Then too?!

217
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:13,811
Always?

218
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:18,816
I do go over to his place if I have to.

219
00:14:18,899 --> 00:14:22,403
And we talk... if we need to.

220
00:14:25,739 --> 00:14:26,991
Normal, huh?

221
00:14:27,825 --> 00:14:29,994
You're acting way more normal, Ryu.

222
00:14:31,537 --> 00:14:35,040
Is this what normal is for us from now on?

223
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:38,711
I need ya to level up for me!

224
00:14:38,794 --> 00:14:41,422
What are you doing in my room
before I even got home?

225
00:14:42,006 --> 00:14:44,592
C'mon, Ryu, you know the deal.
What's yours is mine.

226
00:14:45,551 --> 00:14:47,094
No way. Nope!

227
00:14:48,596 --> 00:14:51,307
I can't talk about
those silly things with him.

228
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:52,433
Not anymore.

229
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:55,311
Is that how it's gonna be between us?

230
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,688
From now until forever?

231
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:00,900
To be honest, I'm confused.

232
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:03,110
I can't make heads or tails of it.

233
00:15:03,736 --> 00:15:07,156
Could it be that this
was all just some sort of dream?

234
00:15:08,574 --> 00:15:09,992
Hmm?

235
00:15:11,118 --> 00:15:13,370
If you're looking for Ryu, he's upstairs.

236
00:15:13,454 --> 00:15:14,955
- I was just leav--
- He say anything?

237
00:15:19,627 --> 00:15:21,295
Here! Give this to him!

238
00:15:21,378 --> 00:15:23,422
- Huh?
- They're sushi rolls, 'kay?

239
00:15:23,505 --> 00:15:24,423
Wha--

240
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:26,091
W-- wait, Yoshida!

241
00:15:27,009 --> 00:15:29,929
I could always tell Ryu anything.

242
00:15:30,804 --> 00:15:33,098
I assumed we'd always be together.

243
00:15:33,682 --> 00:15:35,851
Always... but...

244
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:38,812
If you don't actually
have feelings for Sanada,

245
00:15:38,896 --> 00:15:41,023
you shouldn't hang around
with him so much.

246
00:15:42,816 --> 00:15:44,151
But thinking that...

247
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:47,196
was stupid.

248
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:50,157
This really isn't a dream.

249
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:05,005
It's over, isn't it?

250
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:08,509
The "always" I thought we had.

251
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:18,811
Yoshida told me to give this to you.
Sushi rolls.

252
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:25,818
She also asked if you said anything to me.

253
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:28,070
I assume she meant about your confession.

254
00:16:28,904 --> 00:16:31,407
Sorry. I didn't think.

255
00:16:32,324 --> 00:16:33,158
I said you did.

256
00:16:33,242 --> 00:16:36,537
I don't expect you
to lie for me, Shota.

257
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:43,502
These are frickin' great.

258
00:16:44,128 --> 00:16:46,880
- Does she bring sushi to you often?
- Yeah.

259
00:16:47,506 --> 00:16:49,341
Since third grade.

260
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:52,678
Chizuru, is she doin' okay?

261
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:55,514
Well, she kinda ran off.

262
00:17:09,236 --> 00:17:10,446
Hi, Ryu!

263
00:17:10,529 --> 00:17:12,364
Oh... hi.

264
00:17:12,448 --> 00:17:14,033
Thanks for the food last night.

265
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:15,701
Of course!

266
00:17:15,784 --> 00:17:18,954
Anyway, would you mind bringing this bag
to Chizu for me?

267
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:21,498
She completely forgot about it.

268
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:23,500
Oh. That's not like her.

269
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:26,879
I was surprised too.
She was gone by the time I noticed.

270
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:29,089
And she'd even left her rice balls behind.

271
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:31,633
She left her rice balls?

272
00:17:34,803 --> 00:17:37,097
So the only absence is Yoshida, huh?

273
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:38,390
That brat.

274
00:17:38,474 --> 00:17:41,310
And she never resubmitted
her career questionnaire.

275
00:17:41,393 --> 00:17:42,895
Better not be flakin' on me.

276
00:17:42,978 --> 00:17:44,646
Does she have a cold?

277
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:51,070
Hey. Is that Chizu's bag?

278
00:17:51,153 --> 00:17:51,987
Well...

279
00:17:54,406 --> 00:17:55,657
I see.

280
00:17:55,741 --> 00:17:59,411
It's perfectly normal for Sanada
to have something of Chizu's with him.

281
00:18:00,662 --> 00:18:04,625
Those two...
really are back to normal, then?

282
00:18:04,708 --> 00:18:07,669
He confessed his feelings,
she rejected him,

283
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:09,421
but it's like nothing's changed.

284
00:18:10,464 --> 00:18:13,217
But is that actually possible?

285
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:16,970
Wouldn't that be too much
to handle emotionally?

286
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:20,224
It's beyond what I can imagine.

287
00:18:20,307 --> 00:18:24,311
But maybe those two
have a different kind of special bond.

288
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:28,232
And that's why
they can be totally okay like this?

289
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:33,278
It sure is unusual
for Chizu to be absent like this.

290
00:18:33,362 --> 00:18:35,531
Mmm, do you think she might be sick?

291
00:18:35,614 --> 00:18:37,658
- Wanna stop by on our way home?
- Mm-hmm.

292
00:18:37,741 --> 00:18:39,910
In the meantime,
I'll text her just in case.

293
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:43,956
Sure is lonely
without Chizu today, huh?

294
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:49,878
Do you know why
I'm always watching you... Ayane?

295
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:51,839
What do you want?!

296
00:18:53,006 --> 00:18:55,259
- You don't need to be so wary of me.
- I'm not!

297
00:18:55,342 --> 00:18:57,052
You're just taking it
that way, that's all!

298
00:18:57,136 --> 00:19:00,472
Anyway, I came over here
because I'd like to talk to Sadako.

299
00:19:00,556 --> 00:19:01,598
Oh.

300
00:19:01,682 --> 00:19:02,516
Great!

301
00:19:02,599 --> 00:19:06,353
Then, why don't you two get to talking?
I'll be in the bathroom, see ya!

302
00:19:07,688 --> 00:19:09,898
Is that cool?

303
00:19:10,524 --> 00:19:12,442
If I go talk to Sadako alone?

304
00:19:13,152 --> 00:19:16,321
Oh, that's right.
That's how it works now, huh?

305
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:20,784
You don't need
my permission, Kuronuma,

306
00:19:20,868 --> 00:19:23,120
You're allowed to talk
to whoever you want to.

307
00:19:23,203 --> 00:19:25,164
You're a person, not a thing.

308
00:19:25,247 --> 00:19:26,206
Uh, right.

309
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:27,624
Don't worry!

310
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:30,169
It's not like I'm gonna do
anything weird to her, okay?

311
00:19:30,252 --> 00:19:32,296
- You're right about that!
- Let's go, Sadako.

312
00:19:45,434 --> 00:19:47,853
Being more aware
of how other people feel

313
00:19:47,936 --> 00:19:51,315
means you carry a lot more
of that emotional weight with you, right?

314
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:53,400
- Huh?
- That's how it must be for Ayane.

315
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:58,280
Ah, but there was something else
that I wanted to bring up with you.

316
00:19:58,363 --> 00:20:01,742
I've noticed things seem a little strained
between you and Kazehaya.

317
00:20:01,825 --> 00:20:04,703
So things
really are tense between us, then?

318
00:20:04,786 --> 00:20:07,581
I was hoping it was just me
misreading things again!

319
00:20:07,664 --> 00:20:10,751
I'm sorry.
I figured you must have noticed already.

320
00:20:10,834 --> 00:20:12,002
You're good about that.

321
00:20:12,085 --> 00:20:14,087
Usually, people say that I'm dense.

322
00:20:14,171 --> 00:20:17,424
That's just because you don't
notice things about yourself though.

323
00:20:17,507 --> 00:20:18,592
I wouldn't say dense.

324
00:20:18,675 --> 00:20:21,803
You clearly have a lot on your mind,
so it's easy to miss stuff.

325
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:22,721
You think?

326
00:20:23,305 --> 00:20:26,516
When you assume something
is just your imagination, the truth is,

327
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:28,977
a solid 95% of it is most likely true.

328
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:31,772
Whoa! So 95%!

329
00:20:31,855 --> 00:20:33,815
Yeah, that works for me!

330
00:20:34,816 --> 00:20:36,944
Though from what I picked up
when we were talking,

331
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:39,279
Kazehaya didn't sound all that confident.

332
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:42,366
Either way, there's no question
he's totally crazy about you.

333
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:46,536
When we first met, I used to think that

334
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:49,498
you and Kazehaya lived in completely
different worlds from each other.

335
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:51,166
But that's not the case at all.

336
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:53,252
I think you're right next to each other.

337
00:20:53,752 --> 00:20:56,255
In fact, I don't think
you could be much closer.

338
00:20:56,338 --> 00:20:58,966
But... when you're not facing each other,

339
00:20:59,049 --> 00:21:01,760
you're looking as far off
into the distance as you can.

340
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:06,265
So, yeah, things may be a little weird
between you at the moment,

341
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:09,017
but if you close your eyes
and wait for five seconds, well,

342
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:12,271
I'd bet anything
things will get sorted out. Yeah?

343
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:15,107
I-- I've heard that
somewhere before!

344
00:21:15,190 --> 00:21:17,109
Remember, you need to close your eyes

345
00:21:17,192 --> 00:21:18,485
and count to five.

346
00:21:20,737 --> 00:21:23,657
- Oh, no, thank you!
- So what's the problem?

347
00:21:24,366 --> 00:21:29,162
I finally get it now.
How unbelievably embarrassing.

348
00:21:29,746 --> 00:21:32,374
Sadako, you should be
more confident in yourself.

349
00:21:32,457 --> 00:21:34,084
D'ya know what I mean?

350
00:21:35,335 --> 00:21:37,087
So, c'mon, you've already drawn the eye

351
00:21:37,170 --> 00:21:39,464
of the two hottest guys
in this whole school.

352
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:40,924
Me and Kazehaya.

353
00:21:42,759 --> 00:21:43,885
Oh wow!

354
00:21:43,969 --> 00:21:47,889
So then, you and Kazehaya really are
the two hottest guys in the entire school?

355
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:50,934
Well, yeah. Probably.

356
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:55,772
He just said something mind-blowing to me.

357
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:59,401
When I first talked about
how you should date me,

358
00:21:59,484 --> 00:22:01,069
I wasn't kidding around.

359
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:07,117
You may not actually remember it,
but hey, you had a lot going on then.

360
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:12,331
And, at the time, I just didn't understand
a thing about you.

361
00:22:12,414 --> 00:22:13,582
I'm sorry for all that.

362
00:22:14,750 --> 00:22:18,503
But, it's true that I was intrigued enough
to keep an eye on you.

363
00:22:18,587 --> 00:22:21,673
I simply can't help watching people
I'm fascinated with.

364
00:22:24,593 --> 00:22:26,470
He's looking straight-ahead.

365
00:22:27,679 --> 00:22:29,639
- Hey, I...
- Uh?

366
00:22:29,723 --> 00:22:33,185
I feel... like I've learned
so much about life.

367
00:22:33,268 --> 00:22:34,519
All because of you.

368
00:22:36,063 --> 00:22:37,689
Mmm, I feel the same.

369
00:22:38,231 --> 00:22:41,401
You made me realize things
that weren't even on my radar before.

370
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:42,611
Oo.

371
00:22:42,694 --> 00:22:44,780
Like, "Out of the mouth comes evil."

372
00:22:46,823 --> 00:22:49,159
And how incredibly cute Ayane can be.

373
00:22:51,244 --> 00:22:54,331
I just wanted to get all that
off my chest, ya know?

374
00:22:54,414 --> 00:22:56,750
Yeah, that's much better.

375
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:59,544
Well, gonna see
if I can catch up with Ayane.

376
00:22:59,628 --> 00:23:00,879
Huh. Huh?

377
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:02,297
Huh?!

378
00:23:04,257 --> 00:23:06,676
See you later! Good luck!

379
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:11,807
Hmm. Chizu still isn't replying
to my messages.

380
00:23:12,682 --> 00:23:14,101
- Ayane! Hey!
- Hmm?

381
00:23:14,601 --> 00:23:15,560
I found you!

382
00:23:16,186 --> 00:23:17,479
Where's Sawako?

383
00:23:17,562 --> 00:23:19,898
She was headed back
to the classroom, I think.

384
00:23:19,981 --> 00:23:23,151
You better not have spouted
a bunch of weird stuff at her again.

385
00:23:23,235 --> 00:23:25,320
You sure don't trust me, do ya?

386
00:23:25,404 --> 00:23:27,239
Just stop worrying, okay?

387
00:23:27,322 --> 00:23:29,449
- So what did you talk about?
- Hmm?

388
00:23:29,533 --> 00:23:31,868
I gave her some advice with Kazehaya...

389
00:23:31,952 --> 00:23:35,372
You for real?!
Stop interfering! I mean it!

390
00:23:36,039 --> 00:23:38,375
Leave 'em alone!

391
00:23:38,458 --> 00:23:41,086
Uh! What? What's funny?

392
00:23:41,169 --> 00:23:42,295
Well, actually,

393
00:23:42,379 --> 00:23:45,382
you always seem to be worrying
about other people, Ayane.

394
00:23:45,465 --> 00:23:48,510
Mmm? That couldn't be further
from the truth.

395
00:23:48,593 --> 00:23:51,430
- 'Cause I'm always putting myself first.
- Really?

396
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:54,266
You seem like a real people pleaser
from my perspective.

397
00:23:54,349 --> 00:23:55,392
People pleaser?

398
00:23:55,475 --> 00:23:57,519
- Are you for real?!
- Yeah.

399
00:23:58,311 --> 00:24:00,564
You should try saying that
to any of our classmates.

400
00:24:00,647 --> 00:24:02,774
I mean, if you really wanna laugh.

401
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:05,360
Uh, I will. Sure.

402
00:24:06,570 --> 00:24:07,821
Oh, knock it off.

403
00:24:07,904 --> 00:24:09,281
They're gonna laugh at you.

404
00:24:14,161 --> 00:24:15,662
What's your deal?

405
00:24:16,580 --> 00:24:19,291
Don't you think you're giving me
way too much credit?

406
00:24:19,374 --> 00:24:21,918
No, I'm not. I'm sure.

407
00:24:22,002 --> 00:24:23,712
But it is strange to me.

408
00:24:23,795 --> 00:24:26,423
You're incredibly smart,
and you can read the room.

409
00:24:26,506 --> 00:24:29,092
And I'm convinced
you could handle anything.

410
00:24:29,176 --> 00:24:32,012
So why do you always have
such a low opinion of yourself?

411
00:24:32,554 --> 00:24:33,805
Like, you don't know me.

412
00:24:34,514 --> 00:24:35,974
No one really does.

413
00:24:36,057 --> 00:24:37,267
I'm not that person.

414
00:24:37,350 --> 00:24:38,810
That's not true though.

415
00:24:38,894 --> 00:24:41,313
It's fine. Enough sweet talk.

416
00:24:41,396 --> 00:24:42,856
I'm just not that girl.

417
00:24:42,939 --> 00:24:44,441
That's really not true.

418
00:24:44,524 --> 00:24:46,026
If I were a guy instead,

419
00:24:46,109 --> 00:24:49,070
I think I'd choose
to go out with Chizu or Sawako.

420
00:24:49,154 --> 00:24:50,572
Um, maybe Kurumi.

421
00:24:50,655 --> 00:24:53,325
I bet I could do
a way better job than Kazehaya is.

422
00:24:53,408 --> 00:24:54,618
Hey, Ayane...

423
00:24:54,701 --> 00:24:58,872
Earlier, I told you that
I'd never fallen in love first, right?

424
00:24:58,955 --> 00:25:01,541
But... honestly,

425
00:25:01,625 --> 00:25:05,378
I don't think any of the guys I dated
were that into me at any point either.

426
00:25:06,254 --> 00:25:07,172
But, well,

427
00:25:07,923 --> 00:25:09,841
since I am the way I am,

428
00:25:09,925 --> 00:25:11,384
I guess that's just a given.

429
00:25:12,093 --> 00:25:13,553
It's mutual, right?

430
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:17,807
So, either way, I'd still like to at least
have someone to lean on when I'm lonely.

431
00:25:17,891 --> 00:25:20,018
But you're wrong about that.

432
00:25:29,945 --> 00:25:32,822
Hey, it's fine.

433
00:25:34,074 --> 00:25:35,867
Oh, Miura. For you.

434
00:25:36,785 --> 00:25:37,619
Hmm?

435
00:25:40,038 --> 00:25:42,332
- Makin' some memories?
- We're not!

436
00:25:42,832 --> 00:25:43,750
See ya!

437
00:25:44,668 --> 00:25:47,420
Hey. Go put this
on the bulletin board, will ya?

438
00:25:49,172 --> 00:25:51,341
Wait! I'm talkin' to you, blondie!

439
00:25:51,424 --> 00:25:53,426
She's actually super awkward, huh?

440
00:25:53,510 --> 00:25:55,220
Huh? No way!

441
00:25:55,303 --> 00:25:56,680
She knows what she's doin'.

442
00:25:58,974 --> 00:26:00,517
It's finally over!

443
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:01,643
Let's go home!

444
00:26:03,061 --> 00:26:05,146
I still haven't gotten a reply, but...

445
00:26:05,230 --> 00:26:08,316
If she's asleep,
let's leave her a snack and go home.

446
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:13,989
Yeah. Oh... Oh, uh, Kazehaya,
I'm going with Ayane to Chizu's.

447
00:26:14,072 --> 00:26:16,533
To Yoshida's house? Huh.

448
00:26:18,118 --> 00:26:19,869
I wonder if she's even at home?

449
00:26:20,745 --> 00:26:24,165
- Is there something wrong?
- D-- don't worry about it. It's nothing.

450
00:26:30,922 --> 00:26:33,341
Everything's fine.

451
00:26:36,511 --> 00:26:41,057
- Sawako? Let's go.
- Uh, mm-hmm. Bye.

452
00:26:56,865 --> 00:26:58,450
I'm really hungry.

453
00:27:01,953 --> 00:27:04,623
I just couldn't figure out
a good way to reply.

454
00:27:05,582 --> 00:27:08,460
Sorry, Yano-chin, Sawako.

455
00:27:10,337 --> 00:27:11,588
I've been thinking.

456
00:27:12,255 --> 00:27:13,506
Like, a lot.

457
00:27:13,590 --> 00:27:15,759
But I can't wrap my head around this.

458
00:27:16,343 --> 00:27:17,385
I see.

459
00:27:18,094 --> 00:27:21,264
At times like these, the one I'd talk to,

460
00:27:21,890 --> 00:27:23,308
it was always Ryu.

461
00:27:24,267 --> 00:27:25,769
Here. Rice balls.

462
00:27:27,812 --> 00:27:29,272
You're hungry, aren't ya?

463
00:27:29,356 --> 00:27:31,733
Wha-- Kazehaya! H-- how'd you...

464
00:27:31,816 --> 00:27:33,985
What do you mean? Obviously, Ryu told me.

465
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:37,989
I think she's probably around here.

466
00:27:38,073 --> 00:27:41,117
Sorry, Shota, but could you
bring this to her for me?

467
00:27:47,332 --> 00:27:50,710
I'm sure she's gotten...
really hungry by now.

468
00:27:54,714 --> 00:27:56,466
- Better eat.
- Fine, I will!

469
00:27:59,636 --> 00:28:02,013
What are you all calm
and chill for though, huh?

470
00:28:04,391 --> 00:28:05,308
Seriously though.

471
00:28:05,392 --> 00:28:07,602
You're livin' the sweet life
without a care in the world,

472
00:28:07,686 --> 00:28:10,313
gettin' to be all lovey-dovey
with Sawako forever!

473
00:28:10,980 --> 00:28:13,608
These are so good!

474
00:28:13,692 --> 00:28:15,985
Right, right. Thank you!

475
00:28:16,069 --> 00:28:16,945
Damn it!

476
00:28:17,028 --> 00:28:20,198
When the time comes and I'm reborn,
I'm gonna be you, Kazehaya!

477
00:28:20,281 --> 00:28:21,324
Huh? But why?

478
00:28:21,408 --> 00:28:24,703
'Cause if I could become you...

479
00:28:28,123 --> 00:28:28,998
What?

480
00:28:31,126 --> 00:28:32,168
It's nothing.

481
00:28:35,755 --> 00:28:39,092
Ryu and I could keep being best friends.

482
00:28:40,260 --> 00:28:42,095
So, why did you turn him down?

483
00:28:43,930 --> 00:28:47,058
Yeah. Everyone asks me the same thing.

484
00:28:47,142 --> 00:28:48,101
Dating him?

485
00:28:48,184 --> 00:28:50,353
That would be
the more natural thing to do?

486
00:28:51,813 --> 00:28:54,107
But, in that moment...

487
00:28:54,190 --> 00:28:55,775
Since that person

488
00:28:56,901 --> 00:28:58,236
was always you.

489
00:28:58,820 --> 00:29:02,073
When it sunk in, and I realized
he meant he liked me in that way,

490
00:29:02,824 --> 00:29:05,618
I figured that
I should tell him how I felt.

491
00:29:05,702 --> 00:29:08,037
I've never
thought of you like that.

492
00:29:09,414 --> 00:29:10,331
In the most

493
00:29:11,583 --> 00:29:13,168
honest way possible.

494
00:29:16,129 --> 00:29:18,715
Maybe the relationship we had

495
00:29:19,340 --> 00:29:22,302
only worked the way it did because of Ryu

496
00:29:22,385 --> 00:29:24,053
and his feelings for me.

497
00:29:24,929 --> 00:29:28,975
But, wouldn't that mean
everything I'd held dear till then

498
00:29:29,684 --> 00:29:32,562
never actually existed in the first place?

499
00:29:32,645 --> 00:29:34,689
Didn't that
make you happy though?

500
00:29:35,565 --> 00:29:37,400
Even a little bit?

501
00:29:44,574 --> 00:29:46,409
I never even thought about it.

502
00:29:50,288 --> 00:29:56,002
Hey, Kazehaya, did you know
that Ryu felt like that about me?

503
00:29:56,878 --> 00:30:00,548
No. We almost never talk about
that kind of thing.

504
00:30:00,632 --> 00:30:02,008
I figured though.

505
00:30:02,091 --> 00:30:04,469
He's always being misunderstood, right?

506
00:30:05,220 --> 00:30:06,304
By everyone.

507
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:12,018
But, regardless, it was always obvious
how much he cared about you.

508
00:30:13,019 --> 00:30:15,188
No matter what
those specific feelings were.

509
00:30:15,939 --> 00:30:18,107
It's the exact same for me.

510
00:30:19,150 --> 00:30:20,193
I get it.

511
00:30:22,570 --> 00:30:26,115
Ryu's my best friend
and, like, I'm his older sister.

512
00:30:26,199 --> 00:30:29,118
In other words,
I've thought of him as my younger brother.

513
00:30:29,619 --> 00:30:33,456
Or maybe he's my older brother,
and I'm his younger sister?

514
00:30:34,332 --> 00:30:35,708
Whatever, I don't know.

515
00:30:35,792 --> 00:30:38,253
It honestly didn't matter at all
which way it was.

516
00:30:39,045 --> 00:30:40,129
- Chizu!
- Huh?

517
00:30:44,050 --> 00:30:46,344
Yano-chin. Sawako.

518
00:30:47,345 --> 00:30:49,013
Right. That's my cue.

519
00:30:52,851 --> 00:30:54,435
Thank you, Kazehaya.

520
00:31:01,150 --> 00:31:03,486
Hey, uh, what's going on, you two?

521
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:06,114
There's no fever.

522
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:09,284
We're the ones who wanted to know
what's going on with you.

523
00:31:09,367 --> 00:31:11,452
Kazehaya texted us a little bit ago

524
00:31:11,536 --> 00:31:13,705
to tell us that you were here
on the wharf.

525
00:31:14,205 --> 00:31:15,582
You have a cold, don't you?

526
00:31:15,665 --> 00:31:17,750
You shouldn't be out here
where it's freezing.

527
00:31:17,834 --> 00:31:20,336
Huh? What do you mean?
I don't have a cold.

528
00:31:22,130 --> 00:31:24,799
Uh, I skipped because, uh...

529
00:31:26,593 --> 00:31:28,970
...I didn't want to face Ryu.

530
00:31:29,053 --> 00:31:32,891
Uh, what?
Did something else happen between you two?

531
00:31:32,974 --> 00:31:33,808
No.

532
00:31:33,892 --> 00:31:38,313
But, just yesterday,
you were both so normal.

533
00:31:39,647 --> 00:31:41,065
No, they weren't.

534
00:31:41,566 --> 00:31:43,318
- Not at all!
- Huh?

535
00:31:43,401 --> 00:31:46,863
Because when you weren't wanting to see
or even hang out with Sanada,

536
00:31:46,946 --> 00:31:48,781
I knew that something wasn't right.

537
00:31:50,658 --> 00:31:54,287
Just because it's special
doesn't mean it's magically okay.

538
00:31:56,414 --> 00:31:59,959
I thought... it could still be the same.

539
00:32:01,336 --> 00:32:02,211
You know?

540
00:32:04,589 --> 00:32:07,258
But I was wrong. It can't!

541
00:32:07,342 --> 00:32:09,802
Now... can't go and eat ramen!

542
00:32:10,887 --> 00:32:12,931
We can't play games together anymore!

543
00:32:14,015 --> 00:32:17,810
No more inside jokes
or New Year's shrine visits!

544
00:32:17,894 --> 00:32:20,021
We're not siblings anymore!

545
00:32:24,817 --> 00:32:27,445
It hurts
because he's so important to you.

546
00:32:27,528 --> 00:32:30,949
Chizu, those feelings you just
poured out to us,

547
00:32:31,032 --> 00:32:32,075
does Ryu know?

548
00:32:32,575 --> 00:32:35,244
I'm sure he's picked up on them.

549
00:32:35,328 --> 00:32:36,329
Has he?

550
00:32:37,080 --> 00:32:38,831
Does he know everything about you?

551
00:32:39,832 --> 00:32:42,710
And do you know everything about him?

552
00:32:48,257 --> 00:32:50,551
Of course I've realized it.

553
00:32:51,719 --> 00:32:53,846
How he keeps getting bigger than me.

554
00:32:54,681 --> 00:32:56,766
That he's way taller than me now.

555
00:32:58,309 --> 00:33:02,897
I guess I can see...
there are things I don't know about him.

556
00:33:03,690 --> 00:33:05,149
A lot of things.

557
00:33:10,154 --> 00:33:11,906
Hey! What are you doing?!

558
00:33:11,990 --> 00:33:15,743
I can't believe you two right now!
Oh, you're going to get it!

559
00:33:15,827 --> 00:33:16,661
Goat?

560
00:33:17,412 --> 00:33:20,373
We're gonna get it! We're gonna get it!
Ugh!

561
00:33:20,456 --> 00:33:22,917
I can't believe you did that,
you little...

562
00:33:24,419 --> 00:33:26,921
Someone's in trouble! Here. Rice balls.

563
00:33:29,007 --> 00:33:30,591
Ohhhh!

564
00:33:30,675 --> 00:33:32,301
Eat a lot, okay?

565
00:33:32,385 --> 00:33:34,971
- I love rice balls!
- Uh-huh!

566
00:33:35,972 --> 00:33:38,975
Rice balls are Ryu's
favorite food too, you know.

567
00:33:39,058 --> 00:33:42,979
I'm so sorry about the floor, Tetsu.
Please allow me to pay for it.

568
00:33:43,062 --> 00:33:45,273
Huh? Nah, it's fine!

569
00:33:45,356 --> 00:33:48,609
I mean, if she marries
into our family one day...

570
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:50,987
Chizu, this will be your home.

571
00:33:51,070 --> 00:33:55,283
So, sound good?
You'd be able to have a lot of rice balls.

572
00:33:55,366 --> 00:33:57,452
- Mmm!
- Eat 'em at home!

573
00:33:58,536 --> 00:34:00,079
Hey! I'm home!

574
00:34:00,163 --> 00:34:02,832
- Oh, Chi, you're here.
- Toru!

575
00:34:04,667 --> 00:34:06,627
Ryu, whoa, are you still eating those?

576
00:34:11,132 --> 00:34:13,718
Here we go. Okay, say cheese!

577
00:34:13,801 --> 00:34:14,635
Cheese!

578
00:34:16,095 --> 00:34:18,890
- Look how much they've grown up.
- Isn't that great?

579
00:34:18,973 --> 00:34:21,476
- You're both in the same class.
- Uh-huh.

580
00:34:21,559 --> 00:34:24,020
You better not
break anything in the classroom!

581
00:34:24,103 --> 00:34:25,104
M'kay!

582
00:34:26,355 --> 00:34:28,775
- Uh-oh.
- Hey! Who did that?!

583
00:34:28,858 --> 00:34:30,943
Run!

584
00:34:31,027 --> 00:34:33,404
Have fun, but remember, think of others!

585
00:34:38,951 --> 00:34:42,163
Argh! Arrrgh! Argh!

586
00:34:43,414 --> 00:34:45,958
That girl is such a troublemaker.
For real.

587
00:34:46,042 --> 00:34:48,669
I think her energy
is her greatest quality.

588
00:34:49,295 --> 00:34:52,673
- How's Ryu doing?
- Hmm? I think he's good.

589
00:34:54,383 --> 00:34:58,012
- Oh, hi, I'm home.
- Ryu! How was school today?

590
00:34:58,096 --> 00:34:59,263
It was fun.

591
00:34:59,347 --> 00:35:00,932
I made some rice balls.

592
00:35:02,683 --> 00:35:04,852
That boy's so laid-back.

593
00:35:05,603 --> 00:35:07,688
And he doesn't have a lot to say.

594
00:35:07,772 --> 00:35:10,608
So people tend to misunderstand
how he's feeling.

595
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:15,404
It's impossible for anyone to
really know what Ryu's thinking, ya know?

596
00:35:15,488 --> 00:35:17,740
- Huh?
- And he's a little scary too.

597
00:35:17,824 --> 00:35:19,617
Yeah, and he glares a lot.

598
00:35:20,576 --> 00:35:22,036
Hey, that's not true at all!

599
00:35:22,745 --> 00:35:25,206
Hey, Chizu. You causing trouble again?

600
00:35:26,999 --> 00:35:29,168
But they got it all wrong.

601
00:35:29,252 --> 00:35:32,046
Now, it's time to have our lunch together.

602
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:33,339
Okay!

603
00:35:33,422 --> 00:35:35,591
Look at what mine has!

604
00:35:35,675 --> 00:35:38,594
Wow! It looks so yummy, Micchan!

605
00:35:42,473 --> 00:35:44,475
Oh no! I'm sorry, Ryu!

606
00:35:45,852 --> 00:35:48,146
Lookit! I brought a banana!

607
00:35:48,229 --> 00:35:50,064
Oy! I stepped on something.

608
00:35:50,148 --> 00:35:52,358
A-- a rice ball? How?

609
00:35:56,904 --> 00:35:59,407
R-- Ryu, I'm sorry!

610
00:35:59,490 --> 00:36:02,118
Oh, i-- it's yours?
I'm sorry.

611
00:36:04,620 --> 00:36:06,164
R-- Ryu...

612
00:36:08,749 --> 00:36:09,584
Huh?

613
00:36:14,797 --> 00:36:17,175
Uh, what happened?

614
00:36:17,258 --> 00:36:20,261
Ryu got really mad at me!

615
00:36:20,344 --> 00:36:23,389
- I said I was sorry, but he won't listen.
- Not true!

616
00:36:23,472 --> 00:36:26,976
It's just that he really loves rice balls,
so it made him real sad.

617
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:30,354
When you apologized,
he wasn't able to hear you.

618
00:36:30,438 --> 00:36:31,898
He's not mad at all!

619
00:36:33,858 --> 00:36:35,026
They don't get it.

620
00:36:35,735 --> 00:36:37,486
Ryu's not scary at all.

621
00:36:41,157 --> 00:36:42,742
Here. Have my sushi.

622
00:36:53,211 --> 00:36:55,213
Huh? He's happy.

623
00:36:57,048 --> 00:36:57,965
Thanks.

624
00:36:59,217 --> 00:37:02,470
Maybe he's too nice.
He should get mad more.

625
00:37:02,553 --> 00:37:03,596
But I get it.

626
00:37:04,805 --> 00:37:05,723
I see.

627
00:37:06,766 --> 00:37:11,270
But, hey, isn't it great that Ryu
has you to understand that about him?

628
00:37:14,774 --> 00:37:15,942
I'm so glad.

629
00:37:20,029 --> 00:37:21,864
Whoa! It's awesome!

630
00:37:22,990 --> 00:37:23,866
Mm-hmm.

631
00:37:53,521 --> 00:37:57,733
- What did you write for your wish?
- Please help me get real good at baseball.

632
00:37:57,817 --> 00:37:59,986
- And you?
- Huh? I'm not telling you!

633
00:38:00,069 --> 00:38:03,239
If I say it, then it won't come true.

634
00:38:04,073 --> 00:38:07,118
- Oh, Toru!
- Welcome home!

635
00:38:07,201 --> 00:38:10,246
Oh, hi, Chi.
What did you write on your tanzaku?

636
00:38:10,329 --> 00:38:14,333
He-he-he-he! It's secret!
Toru! Come play with me! Pretty please?!

637
00:38:14,417 --> 00:38:16,877
Please? Please? Please? Please?!

638
00:38:35,604 --> 00:38:38,190
He's amazing, you know? Toru, I mean.

639
00:38:38,274 --> 00:38:41,444
'Cause when we get buns,
he splits the pork and red bean in half!

640
00:38:41,527 --> 00:38:44,238
- Uh?
- C'mon, how can you not get it?

641
00:38:44,322 --> 00:38:45,656
It's totally smart.

642
00:38:45,740 --> 00:38:47,575
That way you get two different buns.

643
00:38:47,658 --> 00:38:50,453
A two for one.
It's a really good deal, ya know?

644
00:38:50,536 --> 00:38:51,912
How is that good?

645
00:38:51,996 --> 00:38:56,375
So, here, you buy a red-bean bun,
and then I'll buy a pork bun.

646
00:38:56,459 --> 00:38:57,960
I wanna get a rice ball.

647
00:38:58,044 --> 00:38:58,878
That's dumb!

648
00:38:58,961 --> 00:39:02,089
Your mom's rice balls are the best ones
in the whole entire world!

649
00:39:02,173 --> 00:39:03,841
You can eat them at home!

650
00:39:06,302 --> 00:39:07,553
To... ru.

651
00:39:39,668 --> 00:39:42,171
Wait, Ryu!

652
00:39:42,963 --> 00:39:44,423
- The pork bun.
- No, it's fine.

653
00:39:45,424 --> 00:39:49,387
But that's how you eat 'em.
You both share the halves.

654
00:39:49,470 --> 00:39:51,305
It's fine!

655
00:39:58,270 --> 00:39:59,814
When he held her hand,

656
00:39:59,897 --> 00:40:02,900
it was different than when he holds mine!

657
00:40:09,365 --> 00:40:12,910
We didn't end up getting home that day
until after it got dark outside.

658
00:40:13,494 --> 00:40:16,789
So, yeah, you can guess
how much trouble we both got into.

659
00:40:18,499 --> 00:40:22,461
But, Ryu gripped my hand
really hard, so hard,

660
00:40:23,045 --> 00:40:26,465
and he just kept walking
and walking forever.

661
00:40:27,967 --> 00:40:30,219
Well, go ahead
and have these for now.

662
00:40:31,887 --> 00:40:35,349
I got really hungry,
and my tears dried up.

663
00:40:35,891 --> 00:40:39,145
After that,
there was no need to cry anymore.

664
00:40:48,320 --> 00:40:51,198
Ryu! Let's go to school!

665
00:40:51,282 --> 00:40:54,243
Wow! Gosh! Chizu!

666
00:40:54,326 --> 00:40:58,038
I wish I could drive you to school,
but my husband needed the car today.

667
00:40:59,874 --> 00:41:02,626
- See ya later.
- You be careful, okay?

668
00:41:03,294 --> 00:41:04,587
Okay, bye.

669
00:41:04,670 --> 00:41:06,213
Uh, hold on, Chizu.

670
00:41:11,385 --> 00:41:13,179
Hmm. Perfect.

671
00:41:13,262 --> 00:41:14,847
I can't breathe.

672
00:41:14,930 --> 00:41:16,807
Great. That means it's tight enough.

673
00:41:19,393 --> 00:41:21,604
Don't get blown away by the wind!

674
00:41:21,687 --> 00:41:22,855
- 'Kay!
- 'Kay!

675
00:41:22,938 --> 00:41:25,274
Hold hands! And don't let go, okay?

676
00:41:25,357 --> 00:41:26,609
- 'Kay!
- 'Kay!

677
00:41:27,359 --> 00:41:29,945
There'll be rice balls for you
when you get home!

678
00:41:30,446 --> 00:41:31,655
- Okay!
- Okay!

679
00:41:37,286 --> 00:41:41,081
That was...
the last time I ever saw Auntie.

680
00:41:45,544 --> 00:41:48,547
She was on her way
to pick up her youngest, her car slipped,

681
00:41:48,631 --> 00:41:50,758
and she crashed into a pole!

682
00:41:50,841 --> 00:41:52,510
It was such
a terrible snowstorm.

683
00:41:52,593 --> 00:41:54,261
I'm sure she couldn't see a thing.

684
00:41:54,345 --> 00:41:56,514
It took so long
for them to find her.

685
00:41:56,597 --> 00:41:59,600
The poor woman.
And she was still so young.

686
00:42:01,185 --> 00:42:02,686
Chizu, go on.

687
00:42:07,358 --> 00:42:08,734
Tetsu!

688
00:42:08,817 --> 00:42:10,819
Tetsuko, Chiaki's here to see you.

689
00:42:28,295 --> 00:42:30,089
Big brother took it!

690
00:42:30,172 --> 00:42:31,674
Hey, stop it!

691
00:42:31,757 --> 00:42:32,800
Wow!

692
00:42:40,057 --> 00:42:41,642
Uh, yeah, but they...

693
00:42:43,310 --> 00:42:46,730
I promise
they don't mean any harm.

694
00:42:48,440 --> 00:42:50,568
Chizu... come here.

695
00:42:58,492 --> 00:43:00,828
The sadness
might feel like too much now,

696
00:43:00,911 --> 00:43:03,289
but things will slowly feel normal again.

697
00:43:04,039 --> 00:43:06,083
That's the way grief tends to work.

698
00:43:06,709 --> 00:43:10,170
Tell Auntie Tetsu,
thank you for everything!

699
00:43:17,011 --> 00:43:19,722
That pain
may not go away completely,

700
00:43:19,805 --> 00:43:21,557
but it will fade over time.

701
00:43:29,982 --> 00:43:31,650
Here you go, Chizu.

702
00:43:31,734 --> 00:43:34,153
You must be hungry. Go ahead and eat.

703
00:43:34,236 --> 00:43:36,238
If you find yourself
getting hungry...

704
00:43:39,450 --> 00:43:41,452
- How is it?
- Good.

705
00:43:42,494 --> 00:43:43,704
I'm glad.

706
00:43:44,455 --> 00:43:48,334
...and pain lets up for just a moment
and you smile,

707
00:43:49,209 --> 00:43:51,462
there's nothing wrong with that, okay?

708
00:43:54,131 --> 00:43:55,924
But... Ryu.

709
00:43:58,177 --> 00:43:59,011
Ryu...

710
00:44:03,265 --> 00:44:05,434
Hey, Ryu! I'm here!

711
00:44:06,727 --> 00:44:08,687
- Mm.
- Oh, Chizu.

712
00:44:08,771 --> 00:44:11,148
Thanks for always coming to fetch him.

713
00:44:11,231 --> 00:44:12,358
Morning, Uncle!

714
00:44:12,441 --> 00:44:13,942
Hey! Wait a sec.

715
00:44:24,244 --> 00:44:26,163
You two be careful, 'kay?

716
00:44:26,246 --> 00:44:27,748
Oh, Uncle!

717
00:44:27,831 --> 00:44:31,210
Tonight, Toru and Ryu
can come have dinner at our place, 'kay?

718
00:44:31,293 --> 00:44:33,253
Sorry for any inconvenience.

719
00:44:33,337 --> 00:44:35,756
Hope you have fun
making your delicious ramen!

720
00:44:35,839 --> 00:44:36,757
I will.

721
00:44:36,840 --> 00:44:38,133
Uh, hey!

722
00:44:40,386 --> 00:44:44,348
Ryu, if you ever have a problem,
come talk to me anytime.

723
00:44:44,431 --> 00:44:46,058
Mmm. I'm okay.

724
00:44:46,684 --> 00:44:49,687
- Poor Ryu. How terrible.
- Yeah.

725
00:44:50,688 --> 00:44:53,315
But, at least he seems the same as usual?

726
00:44:55,401 --> 00:44:57,861
Ryu hasn't cried yet.

727
00:44:58,404 --> 00:45:02,700
- Go on. You boys too. Please!
- And eat your fill, okay?

728
00:45:02,783 --> 00:45:05,494
Ryu,
you can have seconds if you'd like.

729
00:45:05,577 --> 00:45:06,578
Yes, please.

730
00:45:07,705 --> 00:45:09,832
He also never smiles.

731
00:45:09,915 --> 00:45:12,459
What? Why are you so mad, Chizu?

732
00:45:12,543 --> 00:45:13,544
I'm not mad, okay?!

733
00:45:27,474 --> 00:45:28,684
Ryu?

734
00:45:29,268 --> 00:45:33,147
- What's up? You haven't gone to sleep yet?
- Uh-uh. Gotta pee.

735
00:45:36,066 --> 00:45:37,067
Toru?

736
00:45:39,111 --> 00:45:40,696
You're up? The bathroom?

737
00:45:40,779 --> 00:45:43,115
No. I just can't seem to fall asleep.

738
00:45:43,824 --> 00:45:45,909
- Should I turn on the light?
- Nah.

739
00:45:46,577 --> 00:45:49,496
My eyes are used to the dark now.
It would be too much.

740
00:45:56,044 --> 00:45:57,921
You sure do look like Tetsu.

741
00:46:00,674 --> 00:46:02,676
I'm missing her like crazy.

742
00:46:02,760 --> 00:46:04,052
It was all so sudden.

743
00:46:05,137 --> 00:46:05,971
Yeah.

744
00:46:18,609 --> 00:46:20,778
Hey, uh, where are Toru and Ryu today?

745
00:46:21,403 --> 00:46:24,615
Ryu told me he was invited
to eat dinner at his coach's house.

746
00:46:24,698 --> 00:46:26,366
Oh, so he's over there.

747
00:46:26,450 --> 00:46:30,162
I know Toru's got a new girlfriend now,
so I think he's with her.

748
00:46:30,245 --> 00:46:32,790
Ah, does he now? Sounds like him.

749
00:46:32,873 --> 00:46:34,750
Should have expected, huh?

750
00:46:34,833 --> 00:46:37,169
Hey, your girlfriend
hasn't been around lately.

751
00:46:37,252 --> 00:46:39,713
- Did something happen?
- Just leave me alone!

752
00:46:44,259 --> 00:46:45,844
What are you doing, Chizu?

753
00:46:45,928 --> 00:46:48,806
- Want rice balls? I'll make some.
- I'm... fine!

754
00:46:48,889 --> 00:46:50,849
Thank you, dinner was great.

755
00:46:50,933 --> 00:46:53,936
Course. Take care.
Here. Don't forget this.

756
00:46:55,145 --> 00:46:56,230
Appreciated.

757
00:47:12,579 --> 00:47:13,664
Ryu?

758
00:47:14,248 --> 00:47:16,500
- Did you just get home?
- Uh, mm-hmm.

759
00:47:16,583 --> 00:47:17,918
Oh, uh, what's that?

760
00:47:21,338 --> 00:47:23,173
Oh, that's right.

761
00:47:23,257 --> 00:47:25,884
- It's probably meant for you.
- Hmm.

762
00:47:27,010 --> 00:47:28,428
From Chi, huh?

763
00:47:28,512 --> 00:47:31,181
How about we share it
for breakfast tomorrow, 'kay?

764
00:47:33,100 --> 00:47:38,146
But... Shota's family already gave me
something to eat for breakfast tomorrow.

765
00:47:40,107 --> 00:47:42,150
So you should eat that all yourself.

766
00:47:46,655 --> 00:47:47,698
Snow.

767
00:47:55,455 --> 00:47:56,623
It hurts.

768
00:48:00,377 --> 00:48:01,295
Yeah.

769
00:48:04,965 --> 00:48:07,050
Hey, it's just you tonight, Ryu?

770
00:48:07,134 --> 00:48:09,845
Toru told me
he's eating at his girlfriend's again.

771
00:48:09,928 --> 00:48:12,222
Looks good! I'm diggin' in!

772
00:48:14,683 --> 00:48:17,102
SANADA

773
00:48:20,522 --> 00:48:21,899
All right.

774
00:48:21,982 --> 00:48:23,817
Did you get enough to eat, Ryu?

775
00:48:23,901 --> 00:48:26,028
Mm-hmm. Thanks for the meal.

776
00:48:49,051 --> 00:48:49,927
Mm?

777
00:48:54,056 --> 00:48:55,057
Huh?

778
00:48:58,393 --> 00:48:59,519
Huh...

779
00:49:01,855 --> 00:49:02,689
It's for...

780
00:49:04,942 --> 00:49:06,026
you, Ryu.

781
00:49:07,027 --> 00:49:08,070
Oh.

782
00:49:31,385 --> 00:49:33,804
The truth is,
we just couldn't accept it.

783
00:49:36,890 --> 00:49:38,308
It's so strange.

784
00:49:38,976 --> 00:49:40,143
T-- Toru!

785
00:49:40,894 --> 00:49:44,398
Chi... Hey, it's not like we're never gonna
see each other again.

786
00:49:44,481 --> 00:49:46,608
I'll come back to visit you guys, okay?

787
00:49:46,692 --> 00:49:49,444
Mmm. Mmm. Okay, you promise?

788
00:49:51,697 --> 00:49:54,449
Sometimes,
people leave even when they're alive.

789
00:49:54,950 --> 00:49:58,286
Ryu... look after Dad.
I'm counting on you.

790
00:49:59,705 --> 00:50:02,290
And you can't be
with people who are dead.

791
00:50:02,374 --> 00:50:05,293
Both situations leave an empty space...

792
00:50:05,377 --> 00:50:07,963
...but they're totally different.

793
00:50:10,090 --> 00:50:12,759
Even if you end up
never seeing someone again,

794
00:50:13,301 --> 00:50:16,430
simply knowing they're alive
somewhere is enough.

795
00:50:22,686 --> 00:50:25,313
- Toru's gone. Really.
- Mmm.

796
00:50:27,024 --> 00:50:28,066
You know what?

797
00:50:29,026 --> 00:50:31,445
- I'll be your sibling now.
- Wha--

798
00:50:33,238 --> 00:50:35,741
I'm not kidding. I promise.

799
00:50:42,122 --> 00:50:45,208
Chi, take care of Ryu for me, all right?

800
00:50:46,835 --> 00:50:49,171
But... you've got me, Ryu.

801
00:50:52,215 --> 00:50:53,175
Always.

802
00:50:55,135 --> 00:50:58,722
A sibling who's the same age
by your side forever.

803
00:51:04,936 --> 00:51:07,689
So I'm the big brother?

804
00:51:07,773 --> 00:51:09,858
Oh, yeah. Huh?

805
00:51:09,941 --> 00:51:12,736
How come?!
But my birthday comes before yours!

806
00:51:13,403 --> 00:51:14,488
Just a feeling.

807
00:51:15,655 --> 00:51:18,492
Forever... and ever.

808
00:51:19,785 --> 00:51:20,869
Always.

809
00:51:26,208 --> 00:51:29,669
So, yeah, all of this sucks.

810
00:51:31,797 --> 00:51:35,717
I can't make sense of it,
and I don't have a real answer.

811
00:51:36,843 --> 00:51:38,136
But what I do know

812
00:51:38,220 --> 00:51:41,848
is that I need to tell Ryu about
all these mixed-up feelings right now.

813
00:51:43,809 --> 00:51:46,645
We lost someone, and time went on.

814
00:51:47,604 --> 00:51:50,190
Our feelings grew numb,
and we let ourselves forget.

815
00:51:51,233 --> 00:51:55,487
As we move on to a future where
we can smile as if nothing ever happened.

816
00:51:56,279 --> 00:52:00,075
Is that what Ryu... what I... really want?

817
00:52:00,784 --> 00:52:04,162
Today, I didn't bring sushi rolls.
These are my rice balls.

818
00:52:10,919 --> 00:52:14,005
These two are your favorites.
The egg and mayo, and bonito flakes.

819
00:52:14,631 --> 00:52:17,551
That one is salted rice. And pickled plum.

820
00:52:17,634 --> 00:52:18,468
Enjoy.

821
00:52:20,720 --> 00:52:23,431
It's early, but that's
your birthday present.

822
00:52:24,015 --> 00:52:28,353
This year, I tried but... I couldn't
find anything I thought you'd like.

823
00:52:30,438 --> 00:52:32,357
But... you did.

824
00:52:39,948 --> 00:52:43,618
Wh-- why are... you staring?

825
00:52:45,704 --> 00:52:47,956
Don't look at me! Stop!

826
00:52:50,083 --> 00:52:52,085
We haven't been alone together since...

827
00:52:54,421 --> 00:52:55,881
It's embarrassing.

828
00:52:55,964 --> 00:52:58,884
Why did... you have to tell me
that you liked me?!

829
00:52:58,967 --> 00:53:01,136
Once you say it out loud, it's all over!

830
00:53:01,720 --> 00:53:03,847
What we both had together, it's gone!

831
00:53:05,432 --> 00:53:07,392
To me, it was precious!

832
00:53:07,475 --> 00:53:10,854
More than anything else!
Now, it's all gone!

833
00:53:10,937 --> 00:53:13,523
'Cause... whenever I see you now,

834
00:53:13,607 --> 00:53:16,359
I have this strange new thought
cross my mind.

835
00:53:17,027 --> 00:53:19,696
Does this guy really love me
or something--

836
00:53:19,779 --> 00:53:20,655
Believe it, then!

837
00:53:22,699 --> 00:53:23,533
Believe it.

838
00:53:29,956 --> 00:53:33,543
That day, there was no reason
to hold back how I felt.

839
00:53:34,920 --> 00:53:36,713
'Cause I wanted it to end.

840
00:53:37,964 --> 00:53:39,299
So let's end it!

841
00:53:47,349 --> 00:53:50,477
So that this can finally start.

842
00:54:00,987 --> 00:54:02,280
It's December.

843
00:54:02,822 --> 00:54:06,826
The city of Kitahoro
is now covered in snow.

844
00:54:08,870 --> 00:54:11,373
Morning! It's freezing, huh?

845
00:54:26,221 --> 00:54:28,431
Gah!

846
00:54:28,515 --> 00:54:30,183
- Ouch!
- Oh, sorry.

847
00:54:31,101 --> 00:54:32,936
- Huh? Whoa!
- Huh?

848
00:54:33,019 --> 00:54:35,021
- When'd you get here?!
- What do you mean?

849
00:54:39,276 --> 00:54:41,194
Hey, about the other day.

850
00:54:41,278 --> 00:54:42,112
The thing.

851
00:54:42,195 --> 00:54:44,698
- Hmm?
- You know what I mean, that!

852
00:54:45,991 --> 00:54:48,285
So... yeah, thank you.

853
00:54:48,368 --> 00:54:50,328
Have things calmed down now?

854
00:54:50,829 --> 00:54:54,040
Actually, it's worse.

855
00:54:54,624 --> 00:54:57,419
- Really? Glad to hear it.
- What the hell?!

856
00:54:58,086 --> 00:55:01,131
So, anyway, as a small token
of my gratitude,

857
00:55:01,214 --> 00:55:04,301
if you ever have anything troubling you,
I'll lend you an ear.

858
00:55:04,384 --> 00:55:06,136
Wait. You, Yoshida?

859
00:55:06,219 --> 00:55:09,889
Well, yeah! I can totally keep a... uh...

860
00:55:09,973 --> 00:55:11,975
Can't say it, can you, huh?

861
00:55:13,977 --> 00:55:17,272
It's hard to talk about it anyway.

862
00:55:17,355 --> 00:55:20,191
Well, I'm planning on
finding the right time myself.

863
00:55:20,734 --> 00:55:23,028
Huh? So there is something?

864
00:55:28,658 --> 00:55:29,492
Hey.

865
00:55:30,618 --> 00:55:31,453
Hey.

866
00:55:35,874 --> 00:55:40,795
It seems like Chizu's always
got something on her mind these days.

867
00:55:44,007 --> 00:55:46,343
Probably about Sanada.

868
00:55:47,052 --> 00:55:49,137
Huh? That's what he said to you?!

869
00:55:50,138 --> 00:55:52,557
Okay, so what did you do after that?

870
00:55:52,640 --> 00:55:55,226
He ate rice balls. That's it.

871
00:55:55,310 --> 00:55:57,437
Huh? Why rice balls?

872
00:55:58,021 --> 00:55:59,939
Because I brought them over to him.

873
00:56:01,024 --> 00:56:03,276
Since they're his favorite food.

874
00:56:15,080 --> 00:56:18,041
He seemed like
a whole different person to me.

875
00:56:19,125 --> 00:56:23,380
Chizu looked...
so cute and girly just now.

876
00:56:24,089 --> 00:56:25,548
Oh, Chizu.

877
00:56:25,632 --> 00:56:28,510
When it comes to Ryu,
she always gets so upset.

878
00:56:28,593 --> 00:56:32,639
Even if it's over something stupid
no one else would get mad about.

879
00:56:32,722 --> 00:56:35,350
You think that she's even aware of it?

880
00:56:35,433 --> 00:56:37,477
I, uh... I wonder.

881
00:56:37,560 --> 00:56:38,770
Well.

882
00:56:38,853 --> 00:56:40,730
That face tells me she has no clue.

883
00:56:41,481 --> 00:56:42,565
Look at that mouth.

884
00:56:42,649 --> 00:56:45,318
We could just toss in a snack,
and she wouldn't notice.

885
00:56:45,402 --> 00:56:47,153
Uh, no, she could choke!

886
00:56:47,237 --> 00:56:48,571
Oh, don't worry about it.

887
00:56:51,449 --> 00:56:53,451
- Argh!
- I'm awake, okay?!

888
00:56:53,535 --> 00:56:57,163
Sorry. You didn't seem as doom and gloom
as you've been lately.

889
00:56:57,247 --> 00:56:59,707
I thought it'd be fine.

890
00:56:59,791 --> 00:57:02,168
Oh!

891
00:57:02,919 --> 00:57:05,505
Thank goodness! She's feeling better!

892
00:57:09,300 --> 00:57:12,095
So library after school today?

893
00:57:12,178 --> 00:57:13,054
Yes.

894
00:57:13,138 --> 00:57:15,306
Shall we start
with the more general stuff?

895
00:57:15,390 --> 00:57:18,017
- Sure.
- Huh. Wow. Lucky.

896
00:57:18,101 --> 00:57:19,018
A library date?

897
00:57:19,102 --> 00:57:21,354
We're studying for exams!

898
00:57:21,438 --> 00:57:24,441
Exams?
You say some weird things.

899
00:57:24,524 --> 00:57:28,695
- Finals. She means our finals.
- I'll see you later, then, all right?

900
00:57:29,487 --> 00:57:30,655
Yeah.

901
00:57:35,368 --> 00:57:36,494
That's right!

902
00:57:36,578 --> 00:57:39,414
You'll be celebrating Christmas
with Kazehaya this year, huh?

903
00:57:39,497 --> 00:57:42,625
No, I-- I mean,
we haven't talked about it!

904
00:57:42,709 --> 00:57:45,086
Please, there's no way
that's not gonna happen.

905
00:57:45,170 --> 00:57:49,048
You're totally going to spend it together.
It goes without saying.

906
00:57:49,132 --> 00:57:51,092
You have to make up for last year.

907
00:57:51,176 --> 00:57:52,844
I forgot!

908
00:57:53,720 --> 00:57:54,971
I wanna go.

909
00:57:55,054 --> 00:57:57,015
I don't wanna miss out on Christmas.

910
00:57:57,599 --> 00:57:58,600
Then, it's time!

911
00:57:58,683 --> 00:58:01,102
Whatever it takes,
you need to convince your dad!

912
00:58:01,186 --> 00:58:05,064
Because, this year, the two of you...
are boyfriend and girlfriend!

913
00:58:18,286 --> 00:58:20,288
I... I wonder.

914
00:58:20,997 --> 00:58:23,958
It's not like
we've even talked about it at all yet.

915
00:58:24,709 --> 00:58:29,214
But is... is that just something
that couples are expected to do?

916
00:58:29,964 --> 00:58:31,007
I don't know.

917
00:58:32,050 --> 00:58:36,179
Honestly, if I go based on
how things seem between us lately,

918
00:58:36,262 --> 00:58:38,723
it doesn't feel like
we'll be celebrating together.

919
00:58:39,349 --> 00:58:41,851
Sadako, you should be
more confident in yourself.

920
00:58:44,812 --> 00:58:48,274
You're already close.
I think you're right next to each other.

921
00:58:49,275 --> 00:58:52,570
Hmm.
Now that I am this close to him,

922
00:58:52,654 --> 00:58:54,781
I shouldn't be thinking like that anymore.

923
00:59:12,257 --> 00:59:13,091
This year,

924
00:59:14,509 --> 00:59:16,594
we're boyfriend and girlfriend, huh?

925
00:59:31,734 --> 00:59:33,319
Sawako!

926
00:59:34,487 --> 00:59:38,157
Listen up. Your old man has given
a lot of thought to Christmas this year.

927
00:59:38,741 --> 00:59:39,909
Huh?

928
00:59:39,993 --> 00:59:43,246
Then, it's time. Whatever it takes,
you need to convince your dad!

929
00:59:43,329 --> 00:59:44,664
Oh, uh, Dad, I...

930
00:59:44,747 --> 00:59:48,793
This year, you can celebrate Christmas
with everyone. How's that sound?

931
00:59:49,502 --> 00:59:51,087
What do you mean by everyone?

932
00:59:51,170 --> 00:59:53,464
She's with Kazehaya,
so don't you think they should--

933
00:59:53,548 --> 00:59:54,382
Everyone!

934
00:59:54,465 --> 00:59:56,843
I mean like Ayane, Chizu, and...

935
00:59:56,926 --> 00:59:58,386
I'm saying you can go, okay?

936
00:59:58,469 --> 01:00:01,389
You mean it?

937
01:00:01,472 --> 01:00:04,392
Thank you, Dad! Thank you!

938
01:00:04,475 --> 01:00:09,147
We can celebrate as a family
on the 23rd or 25th this year.

939
01:00:09,230 --> 01:00:11,399
Wow, dear, what a big step!

940
01:00:12,025 --> 01:00:16,154
I'm so happy!
That's all I can think!

941
01:00:17,238 --> 01:00:21,159
Because the painful
unrequited feelings from last year

942
01:00:21,242 --> 01:00:23,286
will be mutual this time around.

943
01:00:24,037 --> 01:00:27,373
Lately, I've been thinking
so much about how we are.

944
01:00:27,457 --> 01:00:30,043
About how a boyfriend
and girlfriend should be.

945
01:00:30,585 --> 01:00:32,587
But that's not what's important.

946
01:00:32,670 --> 01:00:35,840
What I want
is to be together with Kazehaya.

947
01:00:36,633 --> 01:00:38,801
Not just to gauge
how he's feeling about us,

948
01:00:39,719 --> 01:00:42,764
but because spending time with him
is what really matters.

949
01:00:43,765 --> 01:00:45,308
When exams are over,

950
01:00:45,391 --> 01:00:48,728
I'll ask Kazehaya
to spend Christmas with me.

951
01:00:51,356 --> 01:00:53,524
- We're done!
- I'm gonna sleep!

952
01:00:53,608 --> 01:00:54,734
Time to party!

953
01:00:54,817 --> 01:00:57,028
Let's get some pork buns
on our way home.

954
01:00:58,029 --> 01:00:59,155
It's over!

955
01:00:59,906 --> 01:01:01,032
- Sawako!
- Uh!

956
01:01:01,115 --> 01:01:06,079
- What are your plans?
- I have to... fulfill the mission before me!

957
01:01:06,162 --> 01:01:09,874
- Yeah! Go get it, girl!
- Right! I'm outta here!

958
01:01:10,750 --> 01:01:11,709
It's over!

959
01:01:11,793 --> 01:01:13,920
This is the moment I've been waiting for!

960
01:01:14,003 --> 01:01:15,129
I'm going to tell him!

961
01:01:16,047 --> 01:01:17,924
Ka-- Kazehaya!

962
01:01:18,966 --> 01:01:20,593
Wanna walk together?

963
01:01:20,677 --> 01:01:22,595
Uh...

964
01:01:24,931 --> 01:01:26,766
Okay. Sure.

965
01:01:27,392 --> 01:01:29,560
- Oh, um, Kazehaya--
- Kuronuma.

966
01:01:29,644 --> 01:01:30,603
Yes?

967
01:01:30,687 --> 01:01:34,691
Listen. Do you... have Christmas plans?

968
01:01:36,150 --> 01:01:37,360
You know what?

969
01:01:37,443 --> 01:01:40,613
This year, I don't have to stay
with my folks.

970
01:01:40,697 --> 01:01:44,075
I already had a talk
with my mom and dad, so...

971
01:01:44,158 --> 01:01:45,493
- So I...
- Great!

972
01:01:46,077 --> 01:01:49,747
It's official. Christmas together.

973
01:01:52,166 --> 01:01:53,084
All of us.

974
01:01:57,839 --> 01:02:00,842
I'll be with Kazehaya for Christmas!

975
01:02:02,635 --> 01:02:03,469
Wait.

976
01:02:05,012 --> 01:02:06,180
With everyone?
